---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/page/PageHero.astro';
import Band from '../components/ui/Band.astro';
import Prose from '../components/page/Prose.astro';
import { staticRow, org } from '../lib/page.js';

const row = staticRow({
  path: '/privacy',
  pageType: 'core',
  title: 'Privacy Policy | MrPackerMover',
  h1: 'Privacy policy',
  metaDescription:
    'How MrPackerMover collects, uses, shares and protects your personal data — and your rights under India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.',
  breadcrumbs: [{ path: '/', anchor: 'Home' }],
});
const o = org();
const legalName = o?.legalName ?? 'the Company';
---

<BaseLayout row={row}>
  <PageHero
    dark
    eyebrow="Legal"
    h1={row.h1}
    intro="What we collect, why we collect it, and the control you have over it — written to India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, and in language you can actually follow."
    breadcrumbs={row.breadcrumbs}
    current="Privacy"
  />

  <Band label="Privacy">
    <Prose>
      <div class="legal-notice">
        <strong>Draft for review.</strong> This template will be finalised with legal counsel before
        launch to reflect our final data practices under the DPDP Act, 2023.
        <span class="muted">Effective date: to be set at launch.</span>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This policy explains how <strong>{legalName}</strong> ({o?.brandName ?? 'MrPackerMover'})
        handles your personal data as the data fiduciary, in relation to this website and our moving
        services in India.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>You give us:</strong> name, phone, email, pickup/drop addresses, move details, and any photos or inventory you share for a quote.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatically:</strong> basic device and usage data (e.g. pages viewed) to keep the site working and improve it.</li>
        <li><strong>During a move:</strong> operational records such as your inventory, coordinator notes and packing photos.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To prepare quotes and carry out your move.</li>
        <li>To coordinate crews, provide status and support, and handle claims or complaints.</li>
        <li>To issue GST invoices and meet legal and tax obligations.</li>
        <li>To improve our services and prevent fraud or misuse.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Consent and legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        We process your data on the basis of your consent and for the legitimate uses permitted under
        the DPDP Act, 2023 — principally to provide a service you have requested. Where we rely on
        consent, you may withdraw it at any time (see section 7); this will not affect processing
        already carried out.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share data only as needed to deliver your move: with our crews and coordinators; with a
        licensed insurer if you opt for transit insurance; and with payment, IT and communications
        providers who process data on our behalf under contract. We may disclose data where required
        by law. <strong>We do not sell your personal data.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes above and to meet legal, tax and
        accounting requirements, after which it is deleted or anonymised.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the DPDP Act, 2023, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access a summary of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
        <li>Correct or update inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
        <li>Request erasure of your data where it is no longer needed.</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent, and nominate another person to exercise your rights.</li>
        <li>Raise a grievance with us (section 10) and, if unresolved, with the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use only the cookies needed to run the site and understand aggregate usage. We keep this
        minimal and do not use intrusive advertising trackers. You can control cookies through your
        browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>9. How we protect your data</h2>
      <p>
        We apply reasonable technical and organisational safeguards to protect your data against loss,
        misuse and unauthorised access. No system is perfectly secure, but we work to limit what we
        collect and who can access it.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Grievance officer</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or to exercise your rights, contact our grievance officer through the
        <a href="/company/contact">contact page</a>. The named officer and direct contact details are
        being finalised before launch and will appear here in full.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect the data of children without
        verifiable parental consent as required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as our practices or the law evolve. Material changes will be posted
        here with a revised effective date.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </Band>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-notice {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-warn-500) 35%, var(--color-line));
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-warn-500) 8%, white);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
  }
  .legal-notice strong {
    color: var(--color-ink-900);
  }
</style>
